{"question": "Tiêu chí lựa chọn tài liệu trong tổng quan hệ thống về kháng sinh toàn thân hỗ trợ điều trị nha chu giai đoạn III và IV quy định những ngôn ngữ nào được đưa vào?", "claim": "Các nghiên cứu được đưa vào tổng quan hệ thống chỉ bao gồm các bài báo xuất bản bằng tiếng Anh, trong khi các nghiên cứu xuất bản bằng ngôn ngữ khác đều bị loại bỏ.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Trong quá trình thực hiện tổng quan hệ thống về việc sử dụng kháng sinh toàn thân hỗ trợ điều trị nha chu giai đoạn III và IV, phác đồ lựa chọn tài liệu yêu cầu chỉ chấp nhận các bài báo xuất bản bằng tiếng Anh. Toàn bộ các nghiên cứu hoặc tài liệu được xuất bản bằng các ngôn ngữ khác đều phải bị loại bỏ nhằm đảm bảo tính đồng nhất của dữ liệu."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "A further limitation is the limited representation of true Stage IV populations. Although the present review was designed to include both Stage III and Stage IV periodontitis, much of the available evidence appears to be derived from patients with Stage III disease. Therefore, the findings should not be interpreted as providing strong Stage IV-specific evidence. This distinction is important because Stage IV periodontitis is characterized by additional functional and restorative complexity."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Only articles published in English were included; studies published in other languages were excluded. Published systematic reviews and meta-analyses were eligible, whereas conference abstracts, protocols, editorials, letters, and other non-peer-reviewed publications were excluded. Systematic reviews without a quantitative meta-analysis were excluded according to the predefined eligibility criteria."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Table 4
The overall certainty of evidence (GRADE) for the association between E. saphenum and periodontitis.
Domain | Decision | Rationale
Upgrading factors | Considered, but insufficient for upgrading | A moderate-to-large unadjusted association estimate (OR = 4.85) * was considered. However, no formal upgrade was applied, as the estimate was derived from a single observational study, while the overall body of evidence remained methodologically heterogeneous and unable to establish temporality."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q2", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "* Unadjusted Odds ratio / bivariate estimate reported by Lafaurie et al. 2023 [18] for the association between the presence of E. saphenum and Stage III–IV periodontitis compared with health, 95% CI 1.99–11.7. It was interpreted as supportive of the direction and magnitude of association."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Low-certainty evidence suggests a positive directional association between E. saphenum and periodontitis, particularly in advanced Stage III–IV disease. However, longitudinal, interventional, and mechanistic studies are required to clarify temporality and determine whether E. saphenum contributes functionally to periodontal dysbiosis or primarily represents a marker of established disease."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Systemic Antibiotics as Adjuncts in Periodontal Therapy for Stage III and Stage IV Periodontitis: An Umbrella Review Aligned with the 2018 World Workshop Classification, with AMSTAR-2 Critical Appraisal", "heading_path": ["Body", "4. Discussion", "4.4. Strengths and Limitations"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Systemic Antibiotics as Adjuncts in Periodontal Therapy for Stage III and Stage IV Periodontitis: An Umbrella Review Aligned with the 2018 World Workshop Classification, with AMSTAR-2 Critical Appraisal", "heading_path": ["Body", "2. Materials and Methods", "2.1. Eligibility Criteria"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Association between Eubacterium saphenum and periodontitis: A systematic review", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Results", "3.5. Quality of studies and risk of bias"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Association between Eubacterium saphenum and periodontitis: A systematic review", "heading_path": ["Abstract", "Conclusions"]}]}
