{"question": "Các bệnh lý viêm khớp thái dương hàm như đau khớp, viêm màng hoạt dịch và viêm bao khớp có những đặc điểm lâm sàng và cơ chế sinh học nào?", "claim": "Đau khớp, viêm màng hoạt dịch và viêm bao khớp là các kiểu hình khớp viêm có biểu hiện đau phụ thuộc vào chức năng, đau sâu vùng trước tai, đau khi chịu lực và dịch khớp thường chứa lượng lớn cytokine và prostaglandin.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Trong các bênh lý viêm khớp thái dương hàm bao gồm đau khớp, viêm màng hoạt dịch và viêm bao khớp, đặc điểm bênh học thể hiện qua các cơn đau tăng lên khi thực hiện chức năng, đau sâu vùng trước tai và đau rõ khi khớp phải chịu lực tác động. Phân tích sinh hóa dịch khớp thường phát hiện nồng độ cao các chất trung gian gây viêm như cytokine và prostaglandin."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "al. 2022). A 10‐year retrospective study found that inflammation around teeth and implants may be linked to increased levels of MMP‐8 and IL‐1β in PISF or GCF (Ramseier et al. 2016). Cytokine IL‐1β has been demonstrated to be present in increased quantities within GCF in patients with periodontitis, with an increased concentration of IL‐1β correlating with increased disease severity (Engebretson et al. 2002; Konopka et al. 2012; Zhong et al. 2007). Another study included in this review found high levels of TNF‐α in vape and cigarette users in comparison to non‐smokers in peri‐implant disease (Al Deeb et al. 2020a). This is consistent with the current body of literature and may suggest increased inflammation and destruction. TNF‐α, IL‐6, and MMP‐8 have been suggested to have a role in accelerating peri‐implant tissue destruction, resulting in alveolar bone loss around dental implants, and"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "there may be higher levels of these inflammatory markers for those who use e‐cigarettes, further increasing their risk of peri‐implant disease (Duarte et al. 2016; Teixeira Neves et al. 2022). Interestingly, one study found that non‐smokers had a statistically, significantly higher level of IL‐4, IL‐9, IL‐10, and IL‐13 in comparison to vape users at 3‐months"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 1
Effects of pharmacological modulation of IL-1.
Modulation | Type effect | Pharmacodynamics | Preclinical studies | Clinical studies
Positive | Immunomodulatory (189, 205, 209, 381–387) | Enhanced immune response | Immunodeficiencies or certain types of tumors. The use of agonists is considered a cytokine-based immunotherapy method aimed at overcoming immunosuppression in the tumor microenvironment Preclinical studies of parenteral administration of an IL-1β receptor antagonist in rats (chronic periodontitis and assessing its effect on IFN-γ and TNF-α expression) | Clinical application of the IL-1β receptor antagonist in patients with moderate chronic periodontitis (assessing its effect on IFN-γ and TNF-α expression)"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Arthralgia, synovitis, and capsulitis represent inflammatory arthrogenous phenotypes in which function-dependent pain, deep preauricular tenderness, and pain on loading are common. Synovial fluid in painful TMJs frequently contains elevated cytokines, prostaglandins, and neuropeptides, supporting a peripheral inflammatory driver. Recurrent inflammation may increase the likelihood of persistent trigeminal nociceptive input, particularly when accompanied by mechanical overload or concurrent myofascial pain.15,16"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "surfaces, and anti-inflammatory effects through prostaglandin inhibition. Neem also demonstrates inhibitory effects on matrix metalloproteinase-2 and MMP-9, both associated with extracellular matrix breakdown in periodontitis. Regular use of neem-based oral care products can decrease plaque formation, prevent cavities, and strengthen immune system function (Gawish et al., 2023)."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Effect of Vaping on Treatment Outcomes in Patients With Gingivitis, Periodontitis, and/or Peri‐Implant Disease: A Systematic Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Molecular cytokine-dependent mechanisms of periodontitis pathogenesis and the potential for pharmacological IL-1 modulation in disease treatment", "heading_path": ["Body", "The role of cytokines in the pathogenesis of periodontitis", "The rоle of individual cytokines in the pathogenesis of periodontitis", "Іnterleukіn-1 (IL-1)"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "The Translational Biology of Temporomandibular Disorder Pain: Mechanisms, Biomarkers, and Therapeutic Perspectives", "heading_path": ["Body", "Introduction", "Clinical and Biological Heterogeneity of TMD Pain"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Traditional medicine and natural product based therapeutics in gingivitis management and microbial interactions", "heading_path": ["Body", "Gingivitis treatment and natural products", "Azadirachta indica (neem)"]}]}
