{"question": "Nhiễm trùng nội nha có thể gây ra các triệu chứng lâm sàng dễ nhầm lẫn với bệnh lý nào và cơ chế lan truyền ra sao?", "claim": "Nhiễm trùng nội nha có thể tạo ra các biểu hiện lâm sàng tương tự như bệnh nha chu, với đường dẫn lưu dịch tiết dọc theo không gian dây chằng nha chu gây khiếm khuyết thăm dò sâu hoặc rò rỉ qua các ống tủy phụ.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Nhiễm trùng nội nha thường biểu hiện các triệu chứng lâm sàng rất giống với bệnh nha chu. Dịch tiết từ ổ nhiễm có thể dẫn lưu dọc theo không gian dây chằng nha chu, tạo ra các khiếm khuyết thăm dò sâu hoặc rò rỉ qua hệ thống ống tủy phụ."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Table 1
List of excluded articles
Number | Author and year | Type of laser | Reason for exclusion
19 | Lan et al., 1996 | Nd: YAG | In- vitro study"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Microneedle-based materials address the issue of poor permeability of traditional drugs by penetrating the gingival mucosal barrier, enabling precise drug delivery to deep periodontal tissues. Polylactic acid (PLA)-based microneedles reinforced with tunicate cellulose nanocrystals (TCNCs) (TCNC-g-PLA@PLA-MNs) are functionalized with polydopamine to load irisin and interleukin-1 receptor antagonist, thereby improving diabetic periodontitis through the dual effects of anti-inflammation and osteogenesis promotion (110). The bilayer microneedle (d-MN@MOF) patch integrates magnesium-based metal-organic frameworks (Mg-MOFs), glucose oxidase (GOX), and a methacrylated gelatin (GelMA)/nano-hydroxyapatite (nHA) substrate. It can not only penetrate the gingiva and reach deep into the periodontal pockets but also reduce local blood glucose levels via GOX (111); meanwhile, Mg-MOFs scavenge reactive"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "oxygen species (ROS) and release magnesium ions to promote angiogenesis, ultimately achieving the synergistic regeneration of periodontal soft and hard tissues. The immune and bone metabolism regulatory network mediated by Zn-V-BGN"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "This transition point is pivotal to interdisciplinary care since endodontic infection can produce manifestations similar to those of periodontal disease [86,98]. Drainage tracts may extend coronally along the periodontal ligament space and cause localized deep probing defects, furcation involvement through accessory canals, or a sinus tract opening in the sulcus. As clinicians focus primarily on probing depth, these manifestations can be mistaken for primary periodontal destruction. Conversely, true periodontal disease may exist simultaneously and ultimately lead to secondary endodontic involvement, further emphasizing the need for a systematic differential diagnosis [99,100]."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "As the main component of dental tissue and bone mineral, nano-hydroxyapatite (nHA) is characterized by its compatibility with the physiological environment. This non-toxic material, which is highly compatible with dental/bone tissue, is frequently utilized as an ingredient of fillers and supplements for bone repair. Wang132 developed an nHA in which a polycaprolactone-co-lactide (PCLLA) elastomer matrix included hydroxyapatite particles that make up traditional hydroxyapatite bone powder. Hydrogen bonds are formed by terminal hydroxyl groups on PCLLA arms and many surface hydroxyl groups on HA, which help to create a cross-linked network. In vitro, PCLLA-NanoHA increased macrophage polarization to the M2 phenotype. In vivo, PCLLA-NanoHA promoted alveolar bone repair like that of standard HA bone powder. In diabetic mice, PCLLA-NanoHA performed better at promoting bone tissue repair than"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q2", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "the widely used HA bone powder. PCLLA-NanoHA regulates the M2 polarization of macrophages via activating the PI3K/AKT and peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor gamma (PPAR) signaling pathways. As a result, a favorable local immunological milieu is created for bone regeneration and"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "The effectiveness of lasers in treatment of dentinal hypersensitivity, a scoping review on lasers parametes and clinical protocols", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Hyperglycemic microenvironment-driven periodontal tissue defects: pathogenic mechanisms and therapeutic advances", "heading_path": ["Body", "The therapeutic advances of diabetes mellitus on periodontal tissue defects", "Innovative therapeutic approaches", "Novel biomaterial therapy"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "From Caries to Periodontal Breakdown: A Biological and Clinical Continuum Linking Cariology, Operative Dentistry, Endodontics, and Periodontology", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Pulpitis: The Central Biological Crossroad", "3.4. Pulpal Necrosis: Gateway to Endodontic Infection and Periradicular/Periodontal Manifestations"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Nanoparticle-Based Drug Delivery Systems for Periodontitis: Antibacterial, Immunomodulatory, and Regenerative Strategies", "heading_path": ["Body", "Nanoparticle-Based Drug Delivery Systems for Periodontitis", "Inorganic Nanoparticles", "Hydroxyapatite-Based Nanocarriers"]}]}
