{"question": "Mối quan hệ nhân quả giữa đái tháo đường týp 1 (T1DM) và bệnh sâu răng vĩnh viễn ở trẻ em là gì?", "claim": "Sau khi điều chỉnh đa kiểm định, mối quan hệ nhân quả giữa đái tháo đường týp 1 và sâu răng vĩnh viễn không có ý nghĩa thống kê.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Phân tích ngẫu nhiên Mendelian ghi nhận không có mối liên quan nhân quả mang ý nghĩa thống kê giữa T1DM và sâu răng vĩnh viễn."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) that showed robust associations with T1DM exposure were identified using a genome-wide significance threshold of P < 1×10-8. To account for linkage disequilibrium (LD), clumping was performed using a window size of 10,000 kb and an r² threshold of < 0.001. The F-statistic was calculated for each SNP, and SNPs with F < 10, indicating weak instrument strength, were excluded from the analysis. In addition, palindromic SNPs with intermediate allele frequencies were removed. The remaining eligible SNPs were subsequently used as genetic instrumental variables in this study (24)."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 2
Study design of each selected study
Drug/Drug class (number of records) | References | Study design
Suplatast tosilate (1) | Murata et al.37 | Case report and review of the literature"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "After adjustment for multiple testing, the causal association between T1DM and permanent dental caries remained statistically non-significant."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "The meta-analysis indicated that the decayed, missing, and filled teeth (DMFT) index for permanent teeth was notably higher in children with T1DM compared to the control group, yielding a pooled standardized mean difference (SMD) of 0.19 (95% CI: 0.06–0.31; I2 = 26.6%). However, the MR analysis did not reveal a significant causal relationship between T1DM and the prevalence of dental caries in children and adolescents (OR = 0.98, 95% CI: 0.94–1.02, P = 0.308)."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Association between type 1 diabetes mellitus and dental caries in children and adolescents: a meta-analysis and Mendelian randomization study", "heading_path": ["Body", "Materials and methods", "Mendelian randomization analysis", "Instrumental variable selection"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Drug-Related Halitosis: A Narrative Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Methods", "Screening and data selection"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Association between type 1 diabetes mellitus and dental caries in children and adolescents: a meta-analysis and Mendelian randomization study", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Mendelian randomization analysis", "Causal effect of T1DM on permanent dental caries"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Association between type 1 diabetes mellitus and dental caries in children and adolescents: a meta-analysis and Mendelian randomization study", "heading_path": ["Abstract", "Results"]}]}
