{"question": "Kết quả đánh giá chất lượng các nghiên cứu trong hệ thống tổng quan về tác động của thuốc lá điện tử gồm bao nhiêu nghiên cứu đạt chất lượng 'tốt'?", "claim": "Có năm trong tổng số sáu nghiên cứu được đánh giá đạt chất lượng 'tốt' nhờ đáp ứng tốt tiêu chí lựa chọn và đảm bảo khả năng so sánh giữa các nhóm.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Đánh giá chất lượng các nghiên cứu trong hệ thống tổng quan về tác động của thuốc lá điện tử cho thấy có năm trên tổng số sáu công trình nghiên cứu đạt tiêu chuẩn chất lượng 'tốt'. Các nghiên cứu này đã đáp ứng nghiêm ngặt tiêu chí lựa chọn mẫu và duy trì khả năng so sánh khách quan giữa các nhóm."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "The principles of anesthesia for the procedure do not differ from those used for the removal of impacted teeth, and the same instruments are used in both cases. When removing a tooth intended for transplantation, it is important to ensure that it is not damaged: maintaining the viability of periodontal cells is crucial; hence, the extraction should be minimally traumatic [18]. In cases of fully erupted teeth, dental forceps as well as elevators are the most commonly used instruments. When dealing with impacted teeth, a gentle osteotomy is performed so that the dental sac is not damaged during the procedure [19]. It is also very important that the time between extraction and replanting the donor tooth is minimal [9] because it determines the number of living periodontal cells, which are a key factor in determining the success of this treatment. The literature includes cases of immediate"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "as well as delayed autotransplantation, since the operator responsible for the treatment is not always able to perform the procedure right after detecting the OAC."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 9 shows that both active interventions produced greater improvements than standard care across all outcomes (negative Δdiff values), with zinc consistently achieving the largest benefits. Compared with the standard, zinc reduced VSC by −65.8 ppb and improved organoleptic scores (−1.0), HALT (−11.0), and OHIP-14 (−3.9), while probiotic also improved these measures but to a lesser extent (e.g., VSC −34.6 ppb; organoleptic −0.6; HALT −5.8; OHIP-14 −2.1). Directly comparing zinc vs. probiotic, zinc provided additional meaningful reductions in VSC (−31.2), organoleptic score (−0.4), HALT (−5.2), and OHIP-14 (−1.8), whereas between-group differences were smaller and borderline for tongue coating, plaque index, and So. moorei (with confidence intervals approaching or crossing 0 for some comparisons)."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "The NOS was selected and modified for assessment of cohort (N = 4), (Al Deeb et al. 2020b; ALharthi et al. 2019; Alhumaidan et al. 2022; Shah et al. 2023) case‐control (N = 1), (AlJasser et al. 2021) and cross‐sectional (N = 1) (Al‐Hamoudi et al. 2020) studies (Tables 3a, 3b, 3c). Five of the six studies received a quality rating of “good” as they adequately addressed the selection criteria, ensured comparability between groups, and clearly defined exposure measures (Al Deeb et al. 2020b; Al‐Hamoudi et al. 2020; ALharthi et al. 2019; Alhumaidan et al. 2022; AlJasser et al. 2021). One study received a quality rating of “fair” due to concerns regarding representativeness, as all e‐cigarette users were former conventional smokers, and the duration between cessation of conventional smoking and initiation of e‐cigarette use was not clearly defined, limiting the reliability of attributing the"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q2", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "observed effects solely to e‐cigarette use (Shah et al. 2023). All five papers received a score of between 7 and 9, indicating high quality and low risk of bias (Al Deeb et al. 2020a, 2020b; Al‐Hamoudi et al. 2020; ALharthi et al. 2019;"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Table 5.
Risk of bias judgement by RoB2.
Study | D1 | D2 | D3 | D4 | D5 | Overall
So Ra Kim, 2023 | Low | Low | Low | Low | Low | Low"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Use of Autotransplantation of Wisdom Tooth in Managing Oroantral Communication", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Autotransplantation—Procedure Description"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Clinical and Microbiological Effects of Streptococcus salivarius K12 Lozenges and Zinc Mouthrinse on Persistent Intra-Oral Halitosis", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Results"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Effect of Vaping on Treatment Outcomes in Patients With Gingivitis, Periodontitis, and/or Peri‐Implant Disease: A Systematic Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Quality Assessment of Included Studies"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Diagnosis-based pathways for conservative and minimally invasive management of temporomandibular disorders: a scoping review", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Result", "3.5 Risk of bias assessment"]}]}
