{"question": "Mức độ ảnh hưởng của tình trạng mòn răng đến chất lượng cuộc sống liên quan đến sức khỏe răng miệng (OHRQoL) ở người cao tuổi như thế nào?", "claim": "Những người cao tuổi có mức độ mòn răng nặng hơn sẽ có điểm số OHIP-49 kém hơn đáng kể, cho thấy nhận thức về sức khỏe răng miệng kém hơn.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "- Nhóm người cao tuổi gặp tình trạng mòn răng mức độ nặng thường ghi nhận điểm số OHIP-49 kém hơn đáng kể.\n- Điều này phản ảnh nhận thức về chất lượng cuộc sống liên quan đến sức khỏe răng miệng bị suy giảm rõ rệt."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "A German study [35] assessed changes in OHRQoL with the German version of the OHIP-49 following full-mouth rehabilitation for moderate to severe tooth wear, comparing ceramic and CAD/CAM composite restorations. Among 29 patients (mean age: 44.6 ± 28.4 years), significant improvements were observed in appearance (p < 0.001), while linguistic limitations showed the least improvement (p < 0.001). No significant differences were found between the two materials in appearance (p = 0.913), oral function (p = 0.349), psychosocial impact (p = 0.419), linguistic limitations (p = 0.303), or orofacial pain (p = 0.347). These results suggest that both materials offer comparable benefits, with esthetics showing the greatest impact on OHRQoL."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 5"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "General characteristics of the included studies DMFS, decayed, missing, and filled surfaces; SIC, significant caries index; DMFT, decayed, missing, and filled teeth; OHIP-14, Oral Health Impact Profile - 14 items; OIDP, Oral Impact on Daily Performances; OHRQoL, oral health-related quality of life; VAS, Visual Analog Scale"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q3", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Benn et al. (2014) [38] | - | OHIP-14 | OHIP-14 scores among individuals with xerostomia were 50% higher than among those without the condition. | Physical limitation, functional limitation"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Similarly, Ngoenwiwatkul et al. [28] examined the relationship between oral health status and OHRQoL in 385 elderly individuals (aged 60–93 years, 107 men and 278 women) in Thailand, using OHIP-49. A 63.6% prevalence of tooth attrition was reported, with a mean OHIP-49 score of 54 ± 26. Individuals with more severe tooth wear had significantly worse OHIP-49 scores, indicating poorer perceived oral health (p < 0.001). The study highlighted that tooth attrition, tooth sensitivity, gingival swelling, and oral ulcers were major contributors to impaired OHRQoL, reinforcing the functional and discomfort-related burden of tooth wear in older adults."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Patient-Reported Outcome Measures in Clinical Practice for Tooth Wear: A Literature Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Results", "3.2. Oral Health Impact Profile (OHIP)", "3.2.2. Tooth Wear and OHIP: The Role of Intervention"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Effect of Dental Caries on Oral Health-Related Quality of Life Among Young Adults: A Systematic Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Review"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Patient-Reported Outcome Measures in Clinical Practice for Tooth Wear: A Literature Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Results", "3.2. Oral Health Impact Profile (OHIP)", "3.2.1. Tooth Wear and OHIP: Epidemiological Perspective"]}]}
