{"question": "Trong tổng số bản ghi ban đầu được sàng lọc về chứng chóng mặt ở bệnh nhân rối loạn thái dương hàm, có bao nhiêu nghiên cứu cuối cùng được đưa vào tổng quan hệ thống và phân tích gộp?", "claim": "Tổng số bản ghi ban đầu xác định từ các cơ sở dữ liệu là 311, sau khi loại bỏ các bản ghi trùng lặp và sàng lọc kỹ lưỡng, cuối cùng có đúng 7 nghiên cứu được đưa vào tổng quan hệ thống.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Quá trình tìm kiếm và sàng lọc tài liệu nghiên cứu về chứng chóng mặt liên quan đến rối loạn thái dương hàm bắt đầu với tổng số 311 bản ghi được xác định từ các cơ sở dữ liệu y khoa. Sau khi tiến hành loại bỏ các bản ghi trùng lặp và áp dụng các tiêu chí sàng lọc nghiêm ngặt, hội đồng nghiên cứu đã chọn lọc ra chính xác 7 nghiên cứu đủ tiêu chuẩn để đưa vào phân tích trong tổng quan hệ thống."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "A key observation in this cohort was the prolonged pre-admission symptom duration (mean: $5.4 \pm 1.8$ days), with most patients presenting between days 5 and 7 after symptom onset. In resource-limited settings, presentation delays are multifactorial, driven by limited financial resources, lack of primary dental care facilities, and initial reliance on self-medication or traditional remedies [8, 14]."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Oral hygiene status was assessed in 14 (60.9%) of the 23 studies for association with the prevalence of dental caries. The Simplified Oral Hygiene Index (OHI-S) was the predominant tool, used in 12 (85.7%) of the studies [4,15,48,49,51–53,60–62,64,65], and one study used the Plaque Index [63]. Most studies that used the OHI-S reported the distribution of participants across categories of good, fair, and poor oral hygiene. One study did not specify its tool for OHI measurement [52], while another presented mean OHI-S scores stratified by urban/rural setting, gender, and age [53]."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Table 2
Main characteristics of included articles
Author and year | Type of laser | Laser parameter | Study design | Control group | Pre-procedure management | Post-procedure management | Number of sessions | Interval of sessions | Measured outcome | Evaluation of DH | Side effect | Conclusion
Pantuzzo 2020 | Diode laser (GaAlAs) | 808 nm wavelength; infrared GaAlAs semiconductor diode laser; applied at a central point on exposed root surface for 60 s; single-point application | Randomized Single-Blinded Clinical Trial | Placebo (gel with acrylic resin block) | Not reported | Not reported | 1 | – | Pain reduction due to dentin hypersensitivity | Evaporative stimulus and tactile stimulus pain assessed using VAS and VRSVAS: immediately, 6 h, 12 h, 24 h after treatment; VRS: immediately, 15 min, and 7 days after treatment | No complications reported | Diode laser therapy was more effective"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q2", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "in reducing dentin hypersensitivity than fluoride or placebo; significant reduction observed for evaporative stimulus (P = 0.002); fluoride showed no significant effect"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Initially, 311 records were identified from databases, while no records were obtained from registers. After removing duplicates (n = 47), 264 records were screened, and 28 were excluded due to full-text unavailability. Of the remaining 236 reports sought for retrieval, 19 were not retrieved, leaving 217 reports assessed for eligibility. A total of 210 reports were excluded due to various reasons, including not meeting the PECO criteria (n = 51), being off-topic (n = 48), being literature reviews (n = 29), scoping reviews (n = 40), or grey literature (n = 42). Ultimately, 7 studies [7, 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30] were included in the review, as illustrated in Fig. 1."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Ludwig’s angina in Somalia: clinical characteristics, emergency management, and outcomes from a tertiary academic referral center", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion", "Symptom duration, presentation delay, and inpatient morbidity"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Oral hygiene practices and dental caries experience in Nigeria: A systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Oral hygiene status, frequency, and devices used for oral hygiene", "Oral hygiene status assessment."]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "The effectiveness of lasers in treatment of dentinal hypersensitivity, a scoping review on lasers parametes and clinical protocols", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Prevalence of dizziness in patients with temporomandibular disorders: a systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Results", "3.1 Study selection process"]}]}
