{"question": "Tỷ lệ mắc sâu răng ở các loại bộ răng tại Nigeria có điểm gì đáng chú ý và khác biệt thế nào so với các khu vực khác?", "claim": "Tỷ lệ mắc sâu răng ở Nigeria khác biệt theo loại bộ răng, với tỷ lệ cao nhất ở răng sữa và thấp nhất ở răng hỗn hợp, đồng thời không tăng theo tuổi như tại Đông Phi hay Đông Địa Trung Hải.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Khảo sát dịch tễ học nha khoa tại Nigeria cho thấy tỷ lệ mắc sâu răng khác biệt rõ rệt theo loại bộ răng, trong đó mức độ cao nhất được ghi nhận ở nhóm răng sữa, thấp nhất ở răng hỗn hợp và không có sự khác biệt lớn so với răng vĩnh viễn. Đặc điểm này tạo ra điểm khác biệt lớn so với xu hướng tăng tỷ lệ sâu răng theo độ tuổi thường thấy ở khu vực Đông Phi hoặc Đông Địa Trung Hải."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Mozo et al. [19] explained that if syringe irrigation is used, it is recommended to not bend the needle or place it too close to the WL and to be gentle in delivering the irrigant so it does not penetrate beyond the periapex."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "The analysis further showed that caries prevalence varied by dentition type, with the highest prevalence in primary dentition and the lowest in mixed dentition. Although the prevalence in primary dentition was slightly higher than in permanent dentition, the difference was not statistically significant. This contrasts with findings from Eastern Mediterranean countries [105] and East Africa [106], where caries prevalence increases with age. Age-related increases in caries may result from cumulative plaque accumulation, age-related reductions in salivary flow and buffering capacity, gingival recession exposing vulnerable root surfaces, increased lifetime exposure to sugary diets, and degradation of dental restorations over time [107–111]. The similarity between primary and permanent dentition in Nigeria therefore warrants further investigation to identify local determinants that may modify"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "these patterns."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Local clinicians report that the use of probiotics in combination with standard therapy reduces the bleeding index by 40% and improves clinical adherence—their effectiveness has been proven as an adjunct to mechanical sanitation. Studies are also being conducted in Ukraine on the use of combined probiotic pastes based on Lactobacillus casei and plant extracts, which have shown a 25% reduction in the frequency of relapses (292, 293). The current trend is the introduction of adjuvant therapy aimed at modifying the body's response—the so-called host modulation. The pathogenesis of periodontitis is characterized by an excessive immune response of the body, and therefore, it is advisable to use host modulators—drugs that reduce the activity of inflammation without suppressing immunity. The most extensively studied and FDA-approved drug in this class is sub-antimicrobial dose doxycycline (20"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q2", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "mg twice daily) (SDD)."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Table 6\nQuality assessment of included studies (risk of bias)\n5 | Was the sample frame taken from an appropriate population base so that it closely represented the target/reference population under investigation? | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Evaluating the Preventive and Therapeutic Roles of Active Irrigation Systems in Root Canal Treatment: A Narrative Review and Critical Appraisal of Theory and Methodology", "heading_path": ["Body", "1. Introduction", "1.2. Types of Irrigation Systems", "1.2.1. Syringe or Conventional Irrigation"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Prevalence of dental caries in the primary, mixed and permanent dentitions in Nigeria: A systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Molecular cytokine-dependent mechanisms of periodontitis pathogenesis and the potential for pharmacological IL-1 modulation in disease treatment", "heading_path": ["Body", "Modern approaches to the complex therapy of periodontitis"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Effect of Dental Caries on Oral Health-Related Quality of Life Among Young Adults: A Systematic Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Review"]}]}
