{"question": "Nghiên cứu đánh giá chất lượng các hướng dẫn thực hành lâm sàng về chấn thương răng (TDIs) đã sử dụng công cụ nào và khung nào để định nghĩa câu hỏi nghiên cứu?", "claim": "Nghiên cứu đánh giá chất lượng hướng dẫn thực hành lâm sàng về chấn thương răng sử dụng công cụ AGREE II và khung SPIDER để xác định câu hỏi nghiên cứu.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Quá trình tổng hợp và phân tích dữ liệu trong các nghiên cứu nha khoa thường áp dụng công cụ AGREE II để đánh giá chất lượng hướng dẫn thực hành lâm sàng, đồng thời sử dụng khung SPIDER nhằm xây dựng và định nghĩa chính xác câu hỏi nghiên cứu về chấn thương răng."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Several included studies reported that a substantial proportion of physical education students were active athletes themselves and had either experienced traumatic dental injuries or witnessed such events during sports activities [27–29, 33]. The percentage of students reporting personal experience with dental injuries ranged from 7% to 35% in most studies [28–30, 32, 33], while one study reported a notably higher incidence of 57.9% [34]. This discrepancy may stem from their inclusion of not only dental trauma but also various other forms of oral injuries, collectively termed orofacial trauma. These injuries were categorized into three distinct types: (i) soft tissue injuries (affecting the cheeks, lips, and tongue), (ii) bone tissue injuries (involving the maxilla and mandible), and (iii) dental injuries (encompassing hard and periodontal tissues of the teeth). Interestingly, there was"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "no statistically significant difference in the frequency of dental trauma among students engaged in different sports modalities [16, 29, 34]. Given that this demographic is statistically more prone to TDIs, it is surprising to note the prevailing lack of awareness, particularly among those who have either experienced or witnessed dental injuries, regarding the proper response procedures, first aid measures, and the correct way to preserve a knocked-out tooth."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "We carried out a systematic quality evaluation of CPGs for TDIs using the AGREE II tool and following a methodology published previously [10, 13]. We used the SPIDER framework to define our research question [16]: Sample – general population (children and adults); Phenomenon of Interest – recommendations for the emergency management or treatment of the consequences of TDIs; Design – clinical practice guideline; Evaluation –guideline quality; Research type – qualitative studies. We published the protocol in the Open Science Framework [17]."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "According to the results shown in Table 1, the recommendations of SECIB and MOHP guidelines are established with a high degree of quality. Conversely, the guidelines from RCSE, SFSCMFCO, and DGMKG require modifications to achieve the necessary level of reliability before they can be recommended. In contrast, the FMDS and NVMKA guidelines do not meet the minimum quality requirements to be recommended according to the AGREE II criteria."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Table 4
Correlation score between the scores for each AGREE II instrument domain and the overall
Analysis | Scope and purpose | Stakeholder involvement | Rigour of development | Clarity of presentation | Applicability | Editorial Independence
p-value | < 0.001* | 0.016* | < 0.001* | 0.333 | 0.226 | 0.014*"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "First aid for sports-related dental trauma: a systematic review of knowledge, attitudes, and educational gaps among physical education students", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Emergency and sequalae management of traumatic dental injuries: a systematic survey of clinical practice guidelines", "heading_path": ["Body", "Materials and methods"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Review of clinical practice guidelines on the diagnosis and treatment of third molars. Evaluation of adherence to AGREE II publication guideline", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Emergency and sequalae management of traumatic dental injuries: a systematic survey of clinical practice guidelines", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "AGREE II score and features of the Guidelines"]}]}
