{"question": "Việc nghiên cứu về chấn thương răng ở trẻ em Arab có giúp ích gì cho thực hành lâm sàng không?", "claim": "Các nghiên cứu về chấn thương răng ở trẻ em Arab hoàn toàn không mang lại giá trị định hướng thực hành lâm sàng hay hoạch định chính sách y tế.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Các báo cáo dịch tễ học về chấn thương răng ở trẻ em tại khu vực Arab đã cung cấp những số liệu thống kê chi tiết về tỷ lệ mắc, loại hình chấn thương phổ biến và các yếu tố nguy cơ liên quan. Những dữ liệu này được thu thập từ nhiều trung tâm nha khoa lớn trong khu vực nhằm mục đích theo dõi tình hình sức khỏe răng miệng cộng đồng."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Generation Y, or Millennials, also known as digital natives, are those born between 1981 and 1996. Technology is part of their everyday lives and their activities are mediated by screens. The concept of on and off is completely integrated into their lives. However, they were not born into it; they migrated to the digital world from the analog one in which they were living. Unlike previous generations, because of the economic crisis, the world requires them to be better trained to get a job, as competition is increasing. As opposed to their parents (Generation X), the digital natives or Generation Y dental students are not satisfied with the world around them, are ambitious, and want to achieve their goals. However, the millennial generation is labeled as being lazy, narcissistic, and spoiled. In fact, in 2014, Time magazine labeled them as the “me‐me‐me generation” [13, 14, 15]."}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Millennials are considered the most racially and ethnically diverse adult generation in history."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "A total of 66 papers were included, retrieved from seven databases, with articles published from 2000 to 2025. The included studies originated from multiple countries, with the majority conducted in China (n = 43). Additional studies were from Saudi Arabia (n = 5), Iran (n = 3), Mexico (n = 3) and United Arab Emirates (n = 2). Furthermore, single studies were identified from Brazil, India, Iraq, Italy, Nepal, Poland, Sao Tome and Principe, Spain, Turkey, and Tunisia. Finally, the specific information is shown in Table 1."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "The prevalence of oral trauma in the Arab population can be better understood by solving these research gaps, which can also help to inform clinical practice, guide policy decisions, and identify areas that require further research."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Al-Jundi et al. reported inadequate knowledge among educational personnel regarding the emergency management of TDIs, with some studies indicating that as few as 1.8% of teachers had received formal training.6,7 Cross-sectional studies conducted in Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Brazil, and several European countries consistently demonstrate that teachers' knowledge scores typically range from 20 to 45%, underscoring the global nature of this knowledge gap.8–11 Despite the documented effectiveness of educational interventions using leaflets and posters in improving teachers' knowledge, the overall knowledge base among schoolteachers remains suboptimal globally.12,13"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Enhancing, Targeting, and Improving Dental Trauma Education: Engaging Generations Y and Z", "heading_path": ["Body", "Characteristics of Generations Y and Z"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "The prevalence of dental caries in the first permanent molars among individuals aged 6–18 years: a systematic review and meta-analysis of studies from Asia, Europe, Africa, and Latin America", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Characteristic of included studies"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Traumatic dental injuries in permanent teeth among Arab children: prevalence, and associated risk factors—a systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Introduction"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Assessment of Schoolteachers' Knowledge and Experience in the Emergency Management of Traumatic Dental Injuries: A Two-center Cross-sectional Study", "heading_path": ["Body", "Introduction"]}]}
