{"question": "Chào bác sĩ, bệnh nhân viêm sàn miệng Ludwig thường có tỷ lệ tăng huyết áp kèm theo như thế nào?", "claim": "Bệnh nhân viêm sàn miệng Ludwig luôn kèm theo chứng tăng huyết áp với tỷ lệ rất cao khoảng 65%.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Nghiên cứu lâm sàng về viêm sàn miệng Ludwig tại Somalia cho thấy tỷ lệ bệnh nhân mắc kèm chứng tăng huyết áp là rất cao, chiếm khoảng 65% tổng số ca bệnh được ghi nhận trong quá trình điều trị tại bệnh viện."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "To address this evidence gap, the present study aimed to evaluate the demographic features, underlying etiology, clinical presentation, emergency management strategies, inpatient complications, length of hospital stay (LOS), and discharge outcomes among patients diagnosed with Ludwig’s angina at a major tertiary referral hospital in Mogadishu, Somalia."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 1
Demographic, clinical, and treatment characteristics of patients with Ludwig’s angina (N = 90)
Characteristic | Category | n (%)
| Hypertension | 0 (0.0)"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "In conclusion, Ludwig’s angina in Somalia predominantly affects young men and arises mainly from odontogenic infection. Although delayed presentation and high inpatient complication rates remain major concerns, favorable outcomes, including zero mortality, were achieved with early antibiotics, careful monitoring, and selective surgical management. These findings emphasize the need for improved dental prevention, earlier referral, standardized documentation, and stronger emergency surgical capacity in Somalia and other resource-limited settings."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "This study provides the first systematic clinical evaluation of Ludwig’s angina in Somalia. The findings demonstrate that Ludwig’s angina in this setting is predominantly driven by untreated odontogenic infections, characterized by marked presentation delays, accompanied by a high rate of inpatient secondary complications, but associated with excellent survival when managed with structured antimicrobial therapy and selective surgical decompression."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Ludwig’s angina in Somalia: clinical characteristics, emergency management, and outcomes from a tertiary academic referral center", "heading_path": ["Body", "Introduction"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Ludwig’s angina in Somalia: clinical characteristics, emergency management, and outcomes from a tertiary academic referral center", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Patient characteristics"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Ludwig’s angina in Somalia: clinical characteristics, emergency management, and outcomes from a tertiary academic referral center", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion", "Study limitations"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Ludwig’s angina in Somalia: clinical characteristics, emergency management, and outcomes from a tertiary academic referral center", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion"]}], "conversation": [{"role": "user", "content": "Chào bác sĩ, tôi nghe nói viêm sàn miệng Ludwig hay đi kèm tăng huyết áp phải không?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Đúng vậy, theo tài liệu thì khoảng 65% bệnh nhân mắc kèm chứng tăng huyết áp."}]}
