{"question": "Liệu pháp sinh học mới nào đã được nghiên cứu nhằm điều trị viêm nha chu đái tháo đường thông qua trục ruột - nha chu?", "claim": "Việc bổ sung lợi khuẩn đường uống làm tăng tính thấm của hàng rào ruột và thúc đẩy sự chuyển vị của vi khuẩn gây bệnh, từ đó làm trầm trọng thêm tình trạng viêm nha chu ở bệnh nhân đái tháo đường.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Các nghiên cứu gần đây đã chỉ ra rằng việc bổ sung một số chủng lợi khuẩn đường uống có thể giúp cải thiện hệ vi sinh vật đường ruột ở bệnh nhân đái tháo đường. Tuy nhiên, các dữ liệu hiện tại vẫn chưa làm rõ được cơ chế tác động cụ thể của các chủng này đối với hàng rào niêm mạc ruột cũng như sự chuyển vị vi khuẩn trong bối cảnh bệnh lý nha chu."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "In addition, gut microbiota modulation has emerged as a promising systemic biotherapeutic strategy for diabetic periodontitis by targeting the gut-periodontium axis. Oral supplementation with probiotics remodels the dysbiotic gut microbiome, strengthens intestinal barrier function, and reduces the translocation of pathogenic bacteria and circulating pro-inflammatory cytokines (102)，modulating the gut-periodontium axis as introduced in Section 3.4."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 1
LEVELS OF SCIENTIFIC EVIDENCE
I | Evidence from several randomised controlled clinical trials, systematic reviews of randomised trials and/or international guidelines
VI | Evidence based on the opinion of recognised experts or expert panels, as indicated in guidelines or consensus conferences, based on the opinion of the panel."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Single-cell sequencing technologies provide an opportunity to dissect cellular heterogeneity in TMD. They allow simultaneous analysis of transcriptomic, epigenetic, and functional states of individual cells within cartilage, subchondral bone, synovium, and immune compartments. By resolving disease-associated cell subsets and transitional states, single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) may uncover pathogenic cell populations and signaling networks, thereby refining mechanistic understanding and enabling precision-based classification of TMD.92,104"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Quality-adjusted life years (QALYs) were the most frequently reported health outcome measure across the included studies and were derived using validated health-related quality of life instruments, including the Child Health Utility 9D (CHU-9D), EuroQol 5 Dimensions (EQ-5D), and Paediatric Quality of Life Inventory (PedsQL) [18,19,22,23,25,26]. QALYs combine both the quantity and quality of life into a single metric, enabling comparisons of cost-effectiveness across different health interventions and disease areas [32,33]. Their widespread use within the included studies reflects their value in informing resource allocation decisions and assessing whether dental interventions provide sufficient health benefits relative to their costs."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Hyperglycemic microenvironment-driven periodontal tissue defects: pathogenic mechanisms and therapeutic advances", "heading_path": ["Body", "The therapeutic advances of diabetes mellitus on periodontal tissue defects", "Innovative therapeutic approaches", "Novel biologic therapy"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Italian guidelines for the prevention and management of dental trauma in children", "heading_path": ["Body", "Levels of evidence"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "The Translational Biology of Temporomandibular Disorder Pain: Mechanisms, Biomarkers, and Therapeutic Perspectives", "heading_path": ["Body", "Translational Animal and in vitro Models of TMD Pain", "Strengths and Limitations of Current Preclinical Models"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Direct, Indirect, and Intangible Costs in the Management of Dental Caries in Children Under 18: A Systematic Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "4. Discussion", "4.5. Measurement of Health Outcomes and Intangible Costs"]}]}
