{"question": "Tỷ lệ phần trăm bệnh nhân có nhiều lần thao tác khi phẫu thuật nhiễm trùng có nguồn gốc răng là bao nhiêu?", "claim": "Tỷ lệ bệnh nhân gặp tình trạng nhiều lần thao tác (multiple attempts) trong nghiên cứu về thời gian đến phòng mổ do nhiễm trùng răng là 10,6%.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Dữ liệu thống kê đặc điểm bệnh nhân cho thấy nhóm có nhiều lần thao tác chiếm 11 trường hợp tương đương 10,6%."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "The C-Pilot File is a stainless-steel K-file with a constant 2% taper that undergoes a specialized heat treatment to increase the instrument’s overall stiffness. Designed specifically for orifice searching and negotiation, it has a rigidity equivalent to that of a file two sizes larger. A unique feature of the C-Pilot is its radiopaque markings on the shaft, which facilitate the confirmation of working length during radiographic assessment. The lineup includes sizes #6, #8, #10, #12.5, and #15."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 1
Summary of categorical patient characteristics and outcomes
Characteristic | Number | Percent
Multiple attempts | 11 | 10.6"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "The seven included studies were published between 1972 and 2015 and comprised six clinical studies6–11 and one retrospective case series.12 Together, they reported on 357 patients and approximately 360 OL lesions. Sako et al.6 treated 60 patients with single or multiple OL lesions by cryotherapy. Bekke and Baart12 reported a single-center experience of six years with cryosurgery for treatment of 90 patients undergoing 121 procedures for a range of benign and malignant oral lesions, of them 24 had OL lesions. Yu et al.7 treated 60 OL lesions in 47 patients with cotton-swab cryotherapy. Kawczyk-Krupka et al.8 compared the clinical outcomes of photodynamic therapy for treatment of 48 OL lesions with those of cryotherapy for treatment of 37 OL lesions. Lin et al.9 treated 60 OL lesions in 54 patients with cryogun cryotherapy. Chen et al.10 used cryogun cryotherapy for treatment of 72"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q2", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "patients with 72 OL lesions and adjacent smoking-induced melanosis. Starzyńska et al.11 reviewed 204 OL patients diagnosed between 1999 and 2009 and treated with topical 0.05% tretinoin (n = 74), cryosurgery (n = 63), or conventional surgery (n = 41). The characteristics, doses, treatment sessions, complete regression rate, and recurrence rate reported in the seven studies are summarized in Table 1."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Allergic diseases, which can manifest as allergic rhinitis, asthma, atopic dermatitis, and other conditions, are considered as priorities for prevention and control by the World Health Organization (WHO) [1]. Their disease burden is rising worldwide due to urbanisation and changes in living conditions [2]. Allergic rhinitis specifically was estimated to affect more than 400 million people worldwide in 2019, with prevalence rates ranging from 10–30% in adults and exceeding 40% in children [3]. Meanwhile, 260 million people are affected by asthma and 129 million by atopic dermatitis in 2021 [4]. Patients with allergic diseases often present with symptoms affecting multiple physiological systems, which complicates management [5]. Beyond their effects on respiratory and skin health, allergic diseases may influence oral health through shared epidemiologic pathways, environmental exposures,"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q2", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "and potential side effects of treatments like reduced salivary flow from antihistamines or corticosteroids [6]."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Clinical Significance and Anatomical Considerations of Apical Patency in Endodontic Therapy: A Comprehensive Review", "heading_path": ["Body", "5. Specialized Files for Apical Negotiation", "5.4. C-Pilot File (VDW, Germany)"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Associations of time to the operating room on outcomes in odontogenic infection", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Efficacy of cryotherapy for oral leukoplakia: A systematic review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Characteristics of included studies"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Association between asthma, allergic rhinitis, atopic dermatitis, and dental caries: evidence from systematic review with meta-analysis and Mendelian randomisation investigation", "heading_path": ["Body"]}]}
